* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-pfd-input-threshold (issue #403, spec row 2 / R-5)
* Dynamic edge-registration ladder for the committed SG13CMOS5L `pfd` REF
* input (../netlist-snapshots/pfd.spice).  @DIR@ deck: the REF @AXIS@ level
* is stepped through a @NSEG@-step ladder (16 cycles per step, every edge in
* a step identical), while the other rail stays clean.  Registration is
* counted on edgedet's OUT -- the `set_up` net, the ~5-gate-delay pulse the
* XD1 inv_hv chain + XN1 nand2_hv composite produces per registered rising
* edge: t_rise_<n> is the n-th set_up rising 50%-of-rail crossing.  With the
* ladder monotone (@LADDER@), the last passing segment locates the level
* where every edge still registers; segment geometry is recomputed by
* threshold_grid.py reduce from the same constants.
*
* FB is driven too -- a full-rail copy at a fixed @FBTD_s@ s offset, exactly
* as sg13g2-pfd-reset-parity drives it -- because inside `pfd` reset asserts
* only when UP and DN are both high: with FB static the first REF edge would
* latch UP and never reset, and an edge-counting measurement would read
* 1-of-N at every level regardless of the input threshold.  FB never changes
* across the ladder, so it is not a second confounding variable.
*
* Ladder shape: segment 1 is always the full-swing control (the cheap bench
* bug guard: a 1-of-N nominal result here is an artifact, not a threshold).
*
* Placeholders are substituted by testbench/threshold_grid.py, which also
* inserts the pre_osdi / num_threads lines and the generated meas block (a
* deck-list unit has no .spiceinit).

.lib $PDK_ROOT/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@

.include pfd_snap.spice

Vdd vdd 0 dc @VDD@
Vref ref 0 pwl(@PWL@)
Vfb  fb  0 pulse(0 @VDD@ @FBTD@ @TR@ @TF@ @PWF@ @TPER@)

Xpfd ref fb up dn vdd 0 pfd

.tran @TSTEP@ @TSTOP@ 0 @TMAX@

.control
run
@MEASBLOCK@
.endc
.end
